<ContentLayout title="About StackGeist" description="Who runs StackGeist, what Keith Casko has built, and how the site labels evidence and handles affiliate links.">
  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / About</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">About StackGeist</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Fixes first. Affiliate links second.</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">StackGeist is built and edited by Keith Casko. It focuses on practical troubleshooting, plus IT home labs and certification decisions for people building an IT career.</p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="cards"><div class="card"><h2>Who writes StackGeist</h2><p><strong>Keith Casko</strong> writes and reviews the site. He is working toward IT support and systems roles and studying for a B.S. in Software Engineering, in progress. His projects include <a href="/labs/active-directory-home-lab/">a Windows Server Active Directory lab</a>, <a href="https://supportlab.casko.dev" rel="noopener">ByteGeist Support Lab</a>, and <a href="/labs/aws-cognito-private-crud-fix/">an AWS serverless app</a>. See the <a href="https://casko.dev" rel="noopener">portfolio</a> and <a href="https://github.com/kcasko" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. Pages distinguish personal use from source-backed research instead of pretending every product was tested.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>How recommendations work</h2><p>Lab pages document systems Keith built. Certification comparison pages are researched from official exam sources. Keith’s own certifications are listed, with verification links, on his <a href="/certs/wgu-software-engineering-degree/">WGU degree page</a>. For gear, each product page states its evidence: “Owned and used” only where Keith has personally purchased and used the product (ownership, not a laboratory test), “Research pending” where specifications haven’t been re-checked, and “Researched” otherwise.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2><p>Some links are affiliate links, and they are marked. As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases, and StackGeist may also earn from other programs. A commission does not change the price you pay.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2 id="evidence-policy">What we verify</h2><p>Ownership records practical familiarity, not a laboratory test. Technical specifications and compatibility claims remain tied to identified sources. Price and stock can change after publication. To report a correction, include the page URL and a supporting source when available; contact <a href="mailto:support@stackgeist.dev">support@stackgeist.dev</a>. Corrections are checked against the evidence, and substantive changes receive a new review date.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>What we avoid</h2><p>No fake urgency, fake reviews, fabricated experience, or lists of products added only because they have an affiliate link.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
